---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_122",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 122,
  "text": "<p> [[339.16]] <b>108. LEIBNIZ FÜR PIERRE DE CARCAVY (?)</p>\n<p> [[339.17]] [Juli 1672.] [107.]</b></p>\n<p> [[340.8]] Otto Gerickius Consul Magdeburgensis Tractatum suum <i>de spatio vacuo</i> promisit multis\n[[340.9]] sane egregiis experimentis refertum. Editus est tandem sub hujus anni initium Amstelodami\n[[340.10]] apud Joh. Jansonium van Waesbergen, et scriptum est mihi Francofurto volumen aliquot\n[[340.11]] exemplarium ab autore mihi missum, amicisque distribuendum, illic appulisse. Sed quia\n[[340.12]] nondum vidi, ea interim quae de experimentis ratiocinationibusque suis mihi dudum transcripsit\n[[340.13]] dicam. Inscripsit librum <i>De Spatio vacuo</i>, quia ejus ope pleraque naturae phaenomena explicare\n[[340.14]] nititur, et vacuum reapse per artem exhiberi posse credit. Nam ultra experimentum ejus jam\n[[340.15]] divulgatum, et ab egregiis viris Boylio primum deinde Hugenio provectum, quo aërem exhaurit,\n[[340.16]] aliud ab eo sumtum est, cujus ope credit procurasse <b>vacuum summum</b> seu spatium omni\n[[340.17]] aëre vacuum, quod ne bullas quidem ullas dare possit; aetherem enim poros penetrantem non\n[[340.18]] admittit, quanquam Vacuum ejus seu Spatium quiddam aetheri simile habere videatur, supponit\n[[340.19]] enim id non esse pure passivum seu receptivum, sed activum, per quod <b>virtutes Mundanae</b>\n[[340.20]] seu viventes quas vocat de corpore in corpus licet dissitum, velut per vehiculum quoddam\n[[340.21]] transferantur. </p>\n<p> [[340.22]] Virtutes, quas vocat Mundanas sunt <b>impulsiva,</b> <b>conservativa,</b> <b>expulsiva,</b> <b>dirigens,</b>\n[[340.23]] <b>vertens,</b> <b>sonans,</b> <b>calefaciens,</b> <b>lucens.</b> Has virtutes Mundanas experimento\n[[340.24]] demonstrat in Globo suo sulphureo, de quo in adjectis ex ejus libro excerptis fusius dictum est.\n[[340.25]] Pluma quam Globus attrahit repellitque, pura, et a partibus grossioribus avulsa esse debet ut\n[[340.26]] quam minimum gravet. Pluma a globo repulsa in aëre libero velut suspensa tenetur, globumque\n[[340.27]] circumagentem sequitur, et quia eandem semper faciem globo obvertit, hinc Gerickius explicare\n[[340.28]] conatur Lunae eandem semper faciem telluri obvertentis circa tellurem lationem. </p>\n<p> [[341.1]] In <Fn><i>Den folgenden Absatz hat Leibniz hierher vorgezogen. Ursprünglich stand er weiter hinten vor dem Absatz</i> Liber ipse.</Fn> literis suis ad me datis annotat ad experimentum Globi sulphurei sumendum multa\n[[341.2]] cautione opus esse, imo ne omnibus quidem attritionem manu factam succedere, illos praesertim\n[[341.3]] eludi, quibus manus sunt molliores operumque inassuetae: necesse est etiam loco\n[[341.4]] minime humido teneri, nec manibus madefactis attrectari. Rationem parandi globi ait a se\n[[341.5]] quidem in libro tactam, non tamen satis explicatam, promittit tamen mihi descriptionem ejus\n[[341.6]] distinctam. </p>\n<p> [[341.7]] Vim Elasticam explicat per aëris seipsum prementis gravitatem, quae ubi ablata est, aër ab\n[[341.8]] alio aëre incumbente antea pressus, se restituit. </p>\n<p> [[341.9]] Habet idem Gerickius Baroscopii quoddam genus sine ullo Mercurio, solo aëre adhibito,\n[[341.10]] qui Virunculum quendam, graduum indicem, sustinet; is virunculus tanto magis descendit,\n[[341.11]] quanto aër exterior est levior. </p>\n<p> [[341.12]] Habet et globum diametri duorum circiter pedum, ex duobus hemisphaeriis cupreis sibi\n[[341.13]] impositis constantem, quae etsi nulla re nisi aëris pressione contineantur, non tamen vel a\n[[341.14]] triginta equis divelli possunt, etsi aëre immisso sponte dilabantur. Observat etiam Hemisphaeria\n[[341.15]] ejusmodi facilius divelli quando aër est minus gravis, seu quando Virunculus ejus profundius\n[[341.16]] descendit. Observat etiam, quod valde notabile est, aërem esse leviorem tempore ventoso,\n[[341.17]] sustineri enim nonnihil, diminuique ejus gravitatem a vento. </p>\n<p> [[341.18]] Liber ipse etsi <i>De Spatio vacuo</i> inscriptus sit, nihilominus de toto Mundi systemate in\n[[341.19]] universum, deque principiis rerum tractat. Autor probat motum terrae, ex Planetis credit quanto\n[[341.20]] quisque minor est, tanto esse Soli propiorem, et maculas proinde esse minimos omnium\n[[341.21]] Planetarum Solique proximos. Aërem nihil aliud esse quam effluvium quoddam, et ut ipse\n[[341.22]] loquitur odorem terrae. Habet et de causis meteororum experimenta quaedam singularia, quibus\n[[341.23]] ventos pluviasque explicat. </p>\n<p> [[341.24]] Experimentum suum de Vacuo applicat ad duos magni momenti usus, construxit enim ejus\n[[341.25]] ope tum sclopetum ventaneum fortissimum novi generis, quod scilicet aëre non ut vulgo\n[[341.26]] compresso, et postea exeunte, sed exhausto et postea intrante vim suam exerit; tum vero\n[[341.27]] Machinam cujus ope ingentia pondera subito elevantur. </p>\n",
  "number": "108.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ FÜR PIERRE DE CARCAVY (?)",
  "date": "[Juli 1672.] [107.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:108. LEIBNIZ FÜR PIERRE DE CARCAVY (?) [Juli 1672.] [107.] Otto Gerickius Consul Magdeburgensis Tractatum suum de spatio vacuo promisit multis sane egregiis experimentis refertum. Editus est tandem sub hujus anni initium Amstelodami apud Joh. Jansonium van Waesbergen, et scriptum est mihi Francofurt...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>